{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -12 collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md; rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|thread|conversation|APPROVE'\"' collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan*r5* collab/*register-wasm*review*; sed -n '15,40p' docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md; sed -n '1290,1305p' docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -12 collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md; rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|thread|conversation|APPROVE'\"' collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan*r5* collab/*register-wasm*review*; sed -n '15,40p' docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md; sed -n '1290,1305p' docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Register images → WebAssembly: implementation plan, revision 5\n\nDate: 2026-10-18. Original source baseline: `c49e565dd60ab6a3611c9c772665eca96d1ecd41`; round-1 findings rechecked against the current working tree (HEAD observed as `c818919d0a3284aba0a99308e7a1dcb7bb092850`). The round-1 evidence is retained as checked in r2; source symbols were rechecked for r3 at the same observed HEAD. This complete revision incorporates the binding owner requirement of 2026-10-18 for native Wasmtime/Wasmer support. It is a plan, not an implementation or a performance claim. Round-3 findings were rechecked against that source baseline for this r4 revision. This r5 revision reconciles the Rust-kernel authority after reading all 1,333 lines. Only the new r5 findings file is written; earlier plans and reviews remain unchanged. The shared traversal changes specified below are future implementation prerequisites, not claims that the current kernel already has canonical traversal order.\n\n## Decision and source precedence\n\nImplement a **compiled register backend with resumable body functions and an explicit trampoline**. Each declared body becomes a wasm function with one local per physical register. Intra-body control initially uses generated `br_table` dispatch; guest calls and returns update explicit machine state and return to the trampoline. No guest continuation ever depends on a wasm activation. Define host services through the versioned plain-data linear-memory IMPORT ABI in §4.1.1. The existing CLJS engine is one conforming embedder; a native service implementation shared by Wasmtime and Wasmer adapters is another. Neither JS nor a browser is required to execute the same emitted binary.\n\nThe toolchain is a JVM Clojure emitter producing deterministic WAT, assembled with WABT and instantiated unchanged by Node/browser, Wasmtime or Wasmer. This is emission from register images, not compilation of ClojureScript to wasm. W0 names exact toolchain pins below; these are implementation acceptance targets, not tools claimed to be installed or tested here. A Rust native embedder implements the ABI and semantic services without invoking Node, embedding a JS engine, or delegating transitions to a CLJS subprocess. Wasmtime is required beside Node from W1; Wasmer joins the release gate by W5. Browser embedding uses the same ABI. JVM and Dart remain semantic reference lanes; binding wasm into their application APIs is separate from the required standalone native embedders.\n\nThe mandatory feature profile is **core wasm 1.0 with mutable globals and the original function table / `call_indirect` facility**: i32/i64/f32/f64, structured control, one non-shared wasm32 memory and one function table per module, single-result functions, active data/element segments. No externref or first-class reference values, typed function references, `call_ref`, `return_call`, WasmGC, bulk-memory/table instructions, multi-value, multi-memory, memory64, SIMD, exceptions, threads, component model or JS string builtins are assumed. The baseline table element kind used by `call_indirect` is not permission to emit the later reference-types instruction set. Copy/clear uses scalar loops; no implicit `memory.copy`, `table.set` or `table.grow` instruction may slip in through optimization. Mutable globals need not cross the import boundary; instance base coordinates can use immutable scalar imports.\n\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.stdout.log:1:{\"conversation_id\":\"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"The Round-2 independent second-architect review has been written to [1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md).\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Round-2 Independent Second-Architect Review: Register-VM Wasm Lowering Plan (R2)\\n\\n- **Reviewed Plan**: [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md)\\n- **Round-1 Review**: [1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md)\\n- **Reviewer**: `gemini-4-argon` (Architect)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Round-1 Finding Resolution Audit (Verified Against Body \\u0026 Source Code)\\n\\nEach of the seven Round-1 findings (`MAJOR-1`..`MAJOR-3`, `MINOR-1`..`MINOR-4`) was audited against both the body of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) (not merely the §0 revision log) and the current implementation in `src/cljc/yin/vm/`.\\n\\n### MAJOR-1 — Empty-`K` `:return` and `:return-result` continuation restore `:pc` preservation\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:return`, line 109), §2.4 (line 132), §3.2 step 5 (line 170), §6 W2 (line 265), §6 W3 (line 271).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - [`return-value`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L428-L436): When `(:continuation state)` is `nil`, the transition produces `(assoc state :value retval :halted? true :parked? false)` while leaving `:pc` unchanged (`(:pc state)`, or `(:pc entry)` when driven from a `:return-result` restore).\\n  - [`restore-continuation-record`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L455-L468): The `:return-result` branch restores `:pc (:pc entry)`, `:frames (:frames entry)`, `:continuation (:continuation entry)`, `:store-of (:store-of entry)`, and `:halted? false` onto `base` before calling `(return-value ... value)`.\\n  - §2.3, §2.4, and §3.2 step 5 in the revised plan now specify this exact sequence and explicitly forbid clobbering `:pc` with `0` or advancing it on empty-`K` `:return`.\\n\\n### MAJOR-2 — Bidirectional synchronization between Clojure VM map fields and wasm linear memory across engine/public seams\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §1.2.1 (\\\"Mandatory map ↔ memory synchronization\\\", lines 52–61), §1.3 (line 67), §4.1 (line 186), §6 W0 (line 254), §6 W1 (line 259), §6 W3 (line 273).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - [`module/gc-roots`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L944-L949) and [`collect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2587-L2614) during `:cell/new` ([engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2720)): `engine/handle-effect` on `:cell/new` collects live heap cells by walking Clojure keys (`:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:value`, `:store`, `:wait-set`, `:run-queue`, `:yin.k/puts`) on the `state` map passed to it.\\n  - [`handle-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2746): Writes `:value` on `state'` and may update `:store`, `:id-counter`, `:wait-set`, `:run-queue`, `:parked?`, `:halted?`, and `:yin.k/*`.\\n  - [register_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L444-L445): Callers mutate Clojure map keys (e.g., `(assoc vm3 :store {...})`) between public steps.\\n  - §1.2.1 now mandates the three-point synchronization contract: (1) export hot wasm state (`:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:value`, `:halted?`, `:parked?`, `:store-of`) to the Clojure map before any `engine/*` call, (2) re-import any mutated Clojure map fields back into wasm state after `engine/*` returns, and (3) import caller-visible Clojure map keys on public entry (`vm/step`, `vm/run`, `vm/eval`, `restore-continuation`) and export before returning.\\n\\n### MAJOR-3 — `:call` `:host-fn` effect completion contract (`payload-of`, `park-entry-fns`, blocked `:pc` advance, post-effect `state` preservation)\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:call`, line 106), §2.4 (\\\"Exact host-function effect completion\\\", lines 125–135), §6 W3 (line 271).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - [`handle-host-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L533-L580), [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L709-L719), and [`module/handle-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L579-L584):\\n    - `payload-of` is constructed at the call site with `:pc (inc site-pc)` and `:reg dst`.\\n    - `park-entry-fns` supplies `:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, and `:module/require` park entries, with `handle-host-effect` falling back to `(or (get park-entry-fns eff-type) (when (= :module/try-require eff-type) (:module/require park-entry-fns)) (when (= :stream/poll eff-type) (:stream/next park-entry-fns)))`.\\n    - On `:blocked? true`, `handle-host-effect` returns `(assoc res-state :pc (inc site-pc))` without calling `return-result`.\\n    - On `:parked? true`, `handle-host-effect` returns `res-state` directly.\\n    - On `:halted? true`, `handle-host-effect` returns `(assoc res-state :value value)` directly.\\n    - Otherwise, `return-result` writes `dst` or calls `return-value` on **`res-state`** (preserving all post-effect mutations to `:store`, `:id-counter`, `:wait-set`, `:run-queue`, `:yin.k/*`, etc.).\\n  - §2.4 captures every branch and fallback rule faithfully.\\n\\n### MINOR-1 — Continuation invocation check order and foreign-continuation error keyword\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED (with code-verified correction from Astra)**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:call`, line 106), §3.2 (line 174), §6 W2 (line 265).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - Astra's refutation of the error keyword in Round 1 is verified against [`engine/operator-kind`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L78-L95): `operator-kind` checks `(and (map? f) (= :continuation (:type f)))` and, when `(not= (:machine f) (:type state))`, throws `(ex-info \\\"Cannot invoke foreign continuation\\\" {:type :yin/uncaught-exception, :exception {:reason :foreign-value, :kind :continuation, ...}})`.\\n  - Next, [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L724) calls [`engine/continuation-argument`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L103-L112), which checks `(= 1 (count args))` and throws `:reason :continuation-arity`.\\n  - Finally, [`check-format!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L730-L732) throws `\\\"Continuation format mismatch\\\"` with `{:expected fmt, :actual format}` on mismatch.\\n  - §2.3, §3.2, and §6 W2 now state this exact three-step check order and exact error payloads.\\n\\n### MINOR-2 — `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` must preserve existing `:registers`, `:frames`, and `:continuation`\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §2.3 (`:return` line 109, `:halt` line 110), §2.4 (line 132), §6 W1 (line 259).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L432) and [register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L745-L747) preserve `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, and `:pc` unchanged on empty-`K` `:return` and `:halt`, only updating `:value`, `:halted? true`, and `:parked? false`.\\n  - §2.3, §2.4, and §6 W1 now state this invariant explicitly.\\n\\n### MINOR-3 — `effects/wait-entry-defect` scope and custody gate (`:yin.k/gate`) preservation\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED (with two code-verified corrections from Astra)**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §1.2 (line 45), §4.2 (line 198), §4.2.1 (\\\"Custody gates are preserved engine semantics\\\", lines 200–210), §4.3 (lines 215–216), §6 W3 (line 273), §6 W4 (line 279).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - [`wait-entry-defect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L345-L384) validates queued `:wait-set` entries only (`:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, `:module/require`).\\n  - Astra's two refutations of Round-1 wording details are verified against [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc):\\n    1. [`engine/issue-number`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L554-L559) increments `:yin.k/issued` (not `:yin.k/next-issue`) on `state` and stamps `:yin.k/issue n` on gated records.\\n    2. [`engine/handle-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2713-L2716) on `:stream/close` calls [`gate-refuse!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L484-L492) (which refuses `:exporting` and `:ended`, returning `:running` when mode is `:running`) and then delegates to [`handle-close`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L744-L761), which under `:running` appends `{:stream-id stream-id, :yin.k/issue n}` to `:yin.k/closes` and returns `nil` without calling `stream/close!`.\\n  - §4.2.1 accurately documents all four `:yin.k/*` state keys (`:yin.k/gate`, `:yin.k/puts`, `:yin.k/closes`, `:yin.k/issued`) and exact gate behavior across `:running`, `:exporting`, and `:ended`.\\n\\n### MINOR-4 — Module attachment base offsets, combined-segment payload reads, and empty-base rows\\n- **Status**: **RESOLVED**\\n- **Plan Body Locations**: §5 (lines 229, 232–234), §6 W4 (line 279).\\n- **Verification**:\\n  - [`attach-module-code`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L184-L227), [`shift-pool`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L135-L146), [`fetch-pool` / `fetch-instr`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L525-L530), and [debruijn_register_effects.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L97-L120):\\n    - `attach-module-code` records `:base-code (count cur-code)` and `:base-pool (count cur-pool)` (so attaching to an empty base yields `{:base-code 0, :base-pool 0}`), shifts module pool `:code` (`+ base-code`) and `:consts` (`+ base-pool`) only when `(or (pos? base-code) (pos? base-pool))`, and increments `:program-version`.\\n    - `fetch-pool` and `fetch-instr` index the combined `:pool` and `:bytecode` vectors at `(:pc state)`.\\n  - §5 and §6 W4 now match this exact attachment and segment-indexing contract.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Full-Document Consistency \\u0026 Regression Check\\n\\nA complete pass over §1–§7 of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) confirmed:\\n- No internal contradictions between the §0 revision log and the normative sections (§1–§7).\\n- The W0–W6 phase gates (§6) incorporate all new synchronization, restore, effect-completion, custody-gate, and module-attachment invariants into concrete parity assertions.\\n- No architectural drift or regressions were introduced during the Round-2 edits.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nAPPROVE\\n\\n### Findings Remaining\\nNone. All 3 MAJOR and 4 MINOR findings from Round 1 have been completely and accurately resolved in the plan body.\\n\\n### Properties Passing Review\\n1. **Execution Boundary \\u0026 Dual-Tier Dispatch**: [`engine/run-loop`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2772-L2797) and [`step-on-stream`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L751-L775) cleanly accommodate a wasm inner hot-loop without forking scheduler, stream, store, or module state.\\n2. **Bidirectional Clojure-Map ↔ Linear-Memory Synchronization**: Export-before-engine-call, re-import-after-engine-call, and public-boundary import/export (§1.2.1) preserve [`module/gc-roots`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L944-L949) during `:cell/new` GC collection ([engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2587-L2614)), preserve `:value` and store/scheduler updates after `engine/handle-effect`, and honor caller `assoc` mutations between steps.\\n3. **Value Representation \\u0026 Two-Level Memory Management**: The 64-bit NaN-boxed / tagged-handle value encoding and split between transient wasm arena allocations and Yin logical heap cells (`:heap`, `:cells`, `engine/collect`) preserve Clojure value equality and deterministic logical GC semantics.\\n4. **Bytecode \\u0026 Instruction Semantics**: All 18 opcodes ([`step-instruction`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L622-L749)), [`resolve-Access`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L477-L513), [`call-WithArgs`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L582-L620), [`return-value`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L428-L436), and [`handle-host-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L533-L580) match the canonical interpreter transition-for-transition, including empty-`K` `:pc` and `:registers`/`:frames`/`:continuation` preservation and post-effect `res-state` propagation.\\n5. **Reified Continuations \\u0026 Portable Format**: Continuation capture ([register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L241-L294)) and [`restore-continuation-record`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L455-L468) preserve `{:type :continuation, :machine :yin.vm/debruijn-register, :format :debruijn-register-v1, :value payload}` bit-for-bit across `:call`, `:park`, and `:return-result` entries, including the exact continuation-invocation validation order (`:foreign-value` -\\u003e `:continuation-arity` -\\u003e `\\\"Continuation format mismatch\\\"`).\\n6. **FFI, Effect Handling, and Custody Gates**: Two-step `:ffi/call` ([register.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L691-L705), [ffi.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc#L307-L351)), `debruijn_register_effects` validation ([`wait-entry-defect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L345-L384) on `:wait-set`), and `:yin.k/gate` custody semantics (`:yin.k/puts`, `:yin.k/closes`, `:yin.k/issued` across `:running`, `:exporting`, and `:ended` in [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L484-L761)) are preserved unchanged.\\n7. **Dynamic Module Attachment**: [`attach-module-code`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L184-L227) base-offset shifting, `:module-Table` recording (including `{:base-code 0, :base-pool 0}` on empty bases), combined-segment `:bytecode`/`:pool` indexing, and `:program-version` cache invalidation are preserved.\\n8. **Phased Delivery \\u0026 Parity Gates (W0–W6)**: Each phase maintains green `clj -M:test` and `bb test:cljs` suites and enforces state-equivalence against the canonical interpreter.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":1624.491027,\"num_turns\":3,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":465444,\"output_tokens\":47860,\"thinking_tokens\":13718,\"cache_read_tokens\":2701801,\"total_tokens\":513304}}\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.stdout.log:2:{\"conversation_id\":\"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"I will read the prompt file and the architectural guidelines to understand the task requirements.\\nI will now read the plan under review (`collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md`) and the orchestrator documentation to understand the context and review conventions.\\nI will check `docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md` to understand how `agy` delegate invocations work.\\nI will read the remainder of `docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md` to check the AGY review-mode invocation rules.\\nI will now read the register VM implementation files (`register.cljc`, `debruijn_register_code.cljc`, and `debruijn_register_effects.cljc`) to verify the plan against the actual source code.\\nI will read the remaining lines of `register.cljc` along with `engine.cljc` and `semantic/derive.cljc`.\\nI will read the remaining sections of `engine.cljc` (lift/lower, scheduling, park/resume, wait-set, FFI, and GC).\\nI will read `values.cljc`, `linker.cljc`, `ffi.cljc`, and `yin/vm.cljc`.\\nI will read the remaining lines of `yin/vm.cljc` and `linker.cljc` to verify `machine-data?`, `empty-state`, and linker admission rules.\\nI will read the register VM and engine design documents (`yin.vm.debruijn.register.md` and `yin.vm.engine.md`).\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":296.655082,\"num_turns\":1,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":351853,\"output_tokens\":10718,\"thinking_tokens\":7087,\"cache_read_tokens\":1022954,\"total_tokens\":362571}}\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:4:The plan author (gpt-6-astra) has responded to your APPROVE WITH CHANGES review and\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:39:End with the verdict: APPROVE, APPROVE WITH CHANGES, or REQUEST CHANGES, with the\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:41:APPROVE WITH CHANGES or REQUEST CHANGES, list only the findings that remain (do not\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.stdout.log:1:{\"conversation_id\":\"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"The independent second-architect review has been written to [`collab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Detailed Audit by Review Area\\n\\n### 1. Semantic Fidelity ([`register.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc), [`debruijn_register_code.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc), [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc))\\n\\n1. **`register-restore` with `:resume-mode :return-result` on empty `:continuation` omits `:pc (:pc entry)` (`MAJOR`)**:\\n   - In [`register.cljc:461-468`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L461-L468), `write-back` restores `:pc (:pc entry)` onto `base` *before* calling `return-transition`:\\n     ```clojure\\n     (if (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\\n       (return-transition (assoc base\\n                                 :pc (:pc entry)\\n                                 :frames (:frames entry)\\n                                 :continuation (:continuation entry)\\n                                 :store-of (:store-of entry)\\n                                 :halted? false)\\n                          val)\\n       ...)\\n     ```\\n   - When `(:continuation entry)` is non-empty, `return-transition` ([`register.cljc:433-454`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L433-L454)) overwrites `:pc` with `(:return-pc frame)`. When `(:continuation entry)` is empty (`[]`, e.g., a tail-call effect in body 0 or a tail call reached via tail calls from body 0), `return-transition` ([`register.cljc:432`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L432)) returns `(assoc vm :halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil)` without touching `:pc` or `:registers`. Consequently, on empty `K`, the halted VM's `:pc` is `(:pc entry)` (`(inc site-pc)`) and its `:registers` remains `(:registers base)`.\\n   - Plan §3.2 step 5 ([`findings.md:147`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L147)) states: *\\\"For return-result restore captured K/frames/store-of then run the ordinary return transition.\\\"* Omitting `:pc (:pc entry)` leaves `:pc` at `(:pc base)` when `K` is empty, breaking `IVMState/control` (`{:pc (:pc vm)}`) and raw `:pc` parity in W2/W3.\\n\\n2. **Bidirectional synchronization between the Clojure VM record map keys and the wasm linear-memory header/shadow (`MAJOR`)**:\\n   - Plan §1.2 ([`findings.md:37-46`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L37-L46)) and §4.1 ([`findings.md:163-168`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L163-L168)) place active execution fields (`pc`, active registers, `frames`, `continuation`, `store-of`, `value`, `halted`, `blocked`) in linear memory and expose `read-state(state)`.\\n   - In [`engine.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc) and [`register_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc), the VM state is manipulated as a persistent Clojure record/map directly — not exclusively through `IVM`/`IVMState` methods:\\n     - `engine/collect` ([`engine.cljc:2541-2603`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2541-L2603)), triggered automatically inside `engine/handle-effect` on `:cell/new` ([`engine.cljc:2605-2614, 2720`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2605-L2614)), calls `module/gc-roots` ([`register.cljc:944-949`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L944-L949)), which reads `[(:continuation vm)]` and `[(:registers vm) (:frames vm)]` directly from the `vm` map. If `:continuation`, `:registers`, and `:frames` are not materialized onto the Clojure `vm` map before `engine/handle-effect` runs, `engine/collect` will trace stale or empty roots and sweep live heap cells.\\n     - `engine/handle-effect` ([`engine.cljc:2746`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2746)) sets `:value (:value result)` on `result-state` for every effect (including non-blocking `:store-put`, `:stream-make`, `:stream-cursor`, `:stream-close`, `:cell/*`, and immediate `:stream-put`/`:stream-next`), and [`register.cljc:558-561, 577-580`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L558-L580) preserves that `:value` on the VM map. If the wasm adapter overwrites `:value` on the Clojure map from its pre-effect linear-memory `value` slot upon returning from a non-blocking `HOST_SERVICE`, `(:value vm)` / `(vm/value vm)` after a non-blocking effect step will be stale (nil instead of the effect result).\\n     - Callers and tests directly read `(:registers vm)` ([`register_test.cljc:292-294, 491`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L292-L294)), `(:pc vm')` ([`register_test.cljc:490`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L490)), and mutate the VM map via `(assoc parked :pc 2 :halted? false)` before calling `(vm/run vm-resumer)` ([`register_test.cljc:444-445`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L444-L445)).\\n   - The plan must require that: (a) the Clojure VM record keys (`:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, `:blocked?`) are materialized on the state map before every `engine/*` call and at every public return (`step`, `run`, `restore`), and (b) wasm entry (`step`/`run`) synchronizes from those Clojure map keys whenever they diverge from the cached linear-memory state header/shadow.\\n\\n3. **`:call` of `:host-fn` returning a `module/effect?` omits blocking and `:park-entry-fns` contract (`MAJOR`)**:\\n   - Plan §2.3 ([`findings.md:95`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L95)) says: *\\\"Host fn: apply registered implementation, check typed effect authorization, route effect through engine; ordinary result writes rd/next or executes return transition for tail.\\\"*\\n   - In [`register.cljc:533-545, 564-580, 709-719`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L533-L580), `run-call-effect` builds `payload = (payload-of vm inst)` at the `:call` site (`site-pc = pc`, `pc = (inc pc)`, `:resume-mode` = `:return-result` if `tail?` else `:write-result`, `:dest` = `nil` if `tail?` else `rd`), passes `{:park-entry-fns (park-entry-fns payload)}` (covering `:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, and `:module/require` — which [`module.cljc:581-584`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L581-L584) also uses as fallback for `:module/try-require`) to `engine/handle-effect`, and then:\\n     - When `blocked?` is `true`, returns `(assoc state :pc (inc pc))` (advancing `:pc` to `pc + 1` on the blocked VM state without writing `rd` or running `return-transition`).\\n     - When `blocked?` is `false` and `tail?` is `true`, runs `(return-transition state value)` on the post-effect `state`.\\n     - When `blocked?` is `false` and `tail?` is `false`, returns `(assoc state :pc (inc pc) :registers (assoc (:registers state) rd value))`.\\n\\n4. **`:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` must preserve `:pc`, `:registers`, and `:frames` on the halted VM (`MINOR`)**:\\n   - In [`register.cljc:432, 745-747`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L745-L747), `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` set `:halted? true, :value val, :store-of nil` and leave `:pc` at the `:halt`/`:return` instruction pc (not `pc + 1`), while retaining the halting body's `:registers` and `:frames` (asserted in [`register_test.cljc:292-295`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc#L292-L295)).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Continuation Correctness\\n\\n- **Multi-shot `:current-continuation`, tail-call `K`, and abortive invocation**:\\n  - Every guest `:call` saves an immutable sparse return frame in `K` and returns `TRANSFER` to the host trampoline before the callee body runs (§2.1, [`findings.md:70-71`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L70-L71)), keeping the native wasm stack at depth 1 during body execution and depth 0 at every trampoline boundary.\\n  - Multi-shot `:current-continuation` works without native stack copying because `:frames`, `:regs`, and `:continuation` in the captured payload are immutable records; invoking a reified continuation multiple times via `:call` ([`register.cljc:729-733`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L729-L733)) abortively replaces `:pc`, `:frames`, `:registers`, `:continuation`, and `:store-of` from the capture without mutating the captured payload.\\n  - Note on `:call` of `:continuation` ([`findings.md:95, 151`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L95)): In [`register.cljc:676, 729-733`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L676), ownership is checked inside `engine/operator-kind` ([`engine.cljc:691-708`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L691-L708)) *before* `engine/continuation-argument` validates the 1-arg arity (`:continuation-arity`). The plan should preserve that exact check order so an unowned continuation called with wrong arity raises `:foreign-continuation`, not `:continuation-arity`.\\n- **Linker §7.3 r6 image membership vs layout equivalence**:\\n  - Correctly analyzed in §3.2 ([`findings.md:142`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L142)), §3.3 ([`findings.md:157`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L157)), and §7 item 2 ([`findings.md:258`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L258)).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Invariant Audit ([`docs/design/datom.world.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/datom.world.md))\\n\\n- **No hidden global state**: Satisfied. Value arenas and linear memories are task-owned and explicitly passed (§1.1–1.2); `id-counter` is the task's counter; module registries and primitive tables remain values in VM state.\\n- **No implicit control flow / no callbacks**: Satisfied. No JS Promises, Asyncify, or browser event callbacks resume a retained wasm activation (§2.1, §4.1). Blocking returns `BLOCKED` to the scheduler.\\n- **No shared mutable state**: Satisfied in principle (§1.2–1.3, §7 item 4), subject to enforcing the bidirectional Clojure-map/linear-memory synchronization in Finding 2 above.\\n- **No layer collapsing**: Satisfied. Interpretation/admission (`register-image-defect`, `body-liveness`, `A → R` derivation) remains separate from wasm code generation and execution.\\n- **No assumed graphs**: Satisfied. CFG construction uses validated instruction tuples and explicit body bounds (§2.2).\\n- **Unitarity (A is the only code identity; AST retrievability)**: Satisfied. Wasm binaries have no code identity, are never published to `dao.jing` or indexed as a format identity, and are cached only as disposable local execution artifacts keyed by `(A, R, abi-version, features)` (§Decision, §5, §7 item 9).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Blocking, Effects, and FFI ([`engine.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc), [`ffi.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc), [`yin.vm.engine.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md))\\n\\n1. **`effects/wait-entry-defect` does not accept `:module/require` / `:module/try-require` wait entries (`MINOR`)**:\\n   - Plan §4.2 ([`findings.md:175`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L175)) states: *\\\"`effects/wait-entry-defect` is an acceptance oracle for newly built waits.\\\"*\\n   - In [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:372-379`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L372-L379), `wait-entry-defect` only recognizes `:ffi-writer`, `:ffi-reader`, `:stream-writer` (`:reason :put`), and `:stream-reader` (`:reason :next`), and rejects any other wait entry with `{:rule :wait-shape}`.\\n   - `:module/require` and `:module/try-require` ([`module.cljc:601-636`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L601-L636)) enqueue wait entries with `:reason :link-request`, `:reason :link-response`, and `:reason :install` (and under custody gate `:running`, `:stream/poll` enqueues `:reason :observe` at [`engine.cljc:2706`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2706)). Scope the `effects/wait-entry-defect` assertion in the test harness to stream (`:put`/`:next`) and FFI (`:call-id`/`:request-sent`) wait entries, and use `effects/continuation-defect` plus link-wait shape assertions for `:link-request`/`:link-response`/`:install`.\\n\\n2. **Custody gates (`:yin.k/gate` / `vm/gate-mode`) across stream effects, FFI, and wait-set polling (`MINOR`)**:\\n   - Plan §2.3 mentions custody gates only for `:resume` ([`findings.md:111`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L111)).\\n   - In [`engine.cljc:2162-2189, 2664-2715`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2162-L2189), [`ffi.cljc:209-218`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc#L209-L218), and [`module.cljc:541, 614-636`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L614-L636), `:yin.k/gate` (`:running`, `:exporting`, `:ended`) also governs `ffi/put-request`, `engine/check-wait-set`, `:stream/cursor`, `:stream/put`, `:stream/poll`, `:stream/close`, and `:module/require`. Explicitly list `:yin.k/gate` (and `:yin.k/next-issue`) among preserved engine state roots in §1.2 and add custody-gate parity cases to W3.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Module Growth ([`register.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc), [`linker.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc), [`yin.vm.linker.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md))\\n\\n- **Component-relative wasm codegen vs combined `:segment` absolute pcs (`MINOR`)**:\\n  - When caching component-relative wasm modules with an instance `base` offset (§5 step 3, [`findings.md:194`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L194)), every pc exported to the Task Header (`pc`, `site-pc`, `return-pc`, and `:closure` `:body-pc`) must have `base` added, and `payload-of` must fetch `inst` from the relocated combined `(:segment vm)` at absolute `(:pc vm)`.\\n  - Also clarify in §5 that `create-vm` with an empty image seeds `:images` with `[[empty-R 0 0]]` ([`register.cljc:139`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L139)) and `attach-image` on an empty-base VM leaves `:halted? true` and `:registers []` unchanged.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 6. Slices and Acceptance ([`corpus.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc), [`register_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc))\\n\\n- The W0–W6 slice progression is falsifiable, appropriately grounded in both [`test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc) and [`test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc), and contains no silent behavior-narrowing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 7. Design Contradictions Verified Against Code\\n\\nAll three implementation-vs-design-doc discrepancies noted in the plan ([`findings.md:15-17`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L15-L17)) were verified against the codebase and confirmed accurate:\\n1. Return frames in [`register.cljc:694-701`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L694-L701) and [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:155-210`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L155-L210) carry no `:segment` or `:hash` (superseding [`docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:864-878`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md#L864-L878) per [`docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md` §7.3 r6/r7](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md#L1538-L1543)), and `write-back` never rewinds code space.\\n2. Ready entries use `:resource-updates` merged into private `:resources` ([`engine.cljc:2301-2310`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2301-L2310), [`debruijn_register_effects.cljc:360`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc#L360)), superseding older `:store-updates` prose in [`docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:911, 953`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md#L911) and [`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:82, 134, 152`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md#L82).\\n3. `vm/machine-data?` ([`vm.cljc:1592-1607`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L1592-L1607)) recursively unwraps kernel-minted `Closure`/`Continuation` values by payload, while `engine/encoder` ([`engine.cljc:980-991`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L980-L991)) refuses continuations with `:yin.k/non-portable` (`:non-canonicalizable`).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nAPPROVE WITH CHANGES\\n\\n- `MAJOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:147` | Semantic fidelity (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:431-432, 461-468`): In `write-back`, `:resume-mode :return-result` sets `:pc (:pc entry)` on `base` before calling `return-transition`. When `(:continuation entry)` is empty (`[]`), `return-transition` halts without modifying `:pc` or `:registers`, so the halted VM's `:pc` is `(:pc entry)` (`(inc site-pc)`), not `(:pc base)`. Plan §3.2 step 5 omits `:pc (:pc entry)` on the `return-result` branch. | Update §3.2 step 5 so `return-result` restores `:pc (:pc entry)`, `:frames (:frames entry)`, `:continuation (:continuation entry)`, `:store-of (:store-of entry)`, and `:halted? false` on `base` (while leaving `:registers` as `(:registers base)`) before running `return-transition`.\\n- `MAJOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:37-46, 163-168` | Engine seam \\u0026 state representation (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:44-70, 944-949`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2541-2614, 2720, 2746`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc:292-295, 444, 490-491`): `engine.cljc` and existing tests read and `assoc` Clojure map keys (`:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, `:blocked?`) directly on the VM record without calling `read-state`. Specifically, `engine/handle-effect` on `:cell/new` triggers `engine/collect` -\\u003e `module/gc-roots`, which reads `(:continuation vm)`, `(:registers vm)`, and `(:frames vm)` directly from the map; `engine/handle-effect` also sets `:value` on `result-state` for non-blocking effects; and `register_test.cljc:444` mutates `(assoc parked :pc 2 :halted? false)` before `vm/run`. | Require in §1.2 and §4.1 that: (1) every exit from wasm to a host service or public return materializes `:pc`, `:registers`, `:frames`, `:continuation`, `:store-of`, `:value`, `:halted?`, and `:blocked?` onto the Clojure VM map before `engine/*` runs, (2) non-blocking host services preserve the `:value` set by `engine/handle-effect` rather than clobbering it from the pre-call wasm header, and (3) wasm entry (`step`/`run`) synchronizes from the Clojure map keys whenever they differ from the cached linear-memory header/shadow.\\n- `MAJOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:95` | Semantic fidelity (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:533-545, 564-580, 709-719`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:581-584`): Plan §2.3 `:call` (`Host fn`) only specifies the non-blocking result transition and omits the `run-call-effect` blocking contract and `:park-entry-fns` wiring. | Specify in §2.3 (`:call` -\\u003e `Host fn`) that when a host function returns a `module/effect?` value after `engine/check-callee-effect!`, the adapter builds `payload = (payload-of vm inst)` (which sets `:resume-mode :return-result` and `:dest nil` when `tail?` is true, else `:write-result` and `:dest rd`), passes `{:park-entry-fns (park-entry-fns payload)}` (covering `:stream/put`, `:stream/next`, and `:module/require`) to `engine/handle-effect`, advances `:pc` to `pc + 1` on the blocked state when `blocked?` is true, and when `blocked?` is false either runs `(return-transition state value)` (if `tail?`) or writes `value` to `rd` at `pc + 1` on `state`.\\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:95, 151` | Continuation invocation check order (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:676, 729-733`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:691-708`): `engine/operator-kind` verifies continuation ownership (`:foreign-continuation`) before `engine/continuation-argument` checks exact 1-argument arity (`:continuation-arity`). | State explicitly in §2.3 and §3.2 that `:call` on a continuation checks ownership via `engine/operator-kind` *before* checking arity via `engine/continuation-argument`.\\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:98-99` | Halted state preservation (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:432, 745-747`, `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc:292-295`): `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` leave `:pc` at the `:halt`/`:return` instruction pc (not `pc + 1`) and retain the halting body's `:registers` and `:frames` on the halted VM. | Clarify in §2.3 (`:return` and `:halt`) that halting leaves `:pc` at the halting instruction pc and preserves the active body's `:registers` and `:frames` on the halted VM state.\\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:175, 233` | Wait-entry oracle scope \\u0026 custody gates (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:372-379`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2162-2189, 2664-2715`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi.cljc:209-218`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:601-636`): `effects/wait-entry-defect` only accepts the four R2 stream/FFI shapes and returns `{:rule :wait-shape}` for `:link-request`, `:link-response`, `:install`, and gated `:observe` wait entries; also `:yin.k/gate` custody-gate behavior across stream effects, FFI `put-request`, and `check-wait-set` is not listed in W3. | Scope `effects/wait-entry-defect` in §4.2 to stream (`:put`/`:next`) and FFI (`:call-id`/`:request-sent`) wait entries (using `effects/continuation-defect` + link-wait shape checks for module require waits), and include `:yin.k/gate` custody-gate parity cases in W3.\\n- `MINOR` | `collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:193-198, 239` | Module attachment details (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:139, 192-227`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc:84-120`): When caching component-relative wasm modules with an instance `base` offset, `effects/continuation-payload` still requires the relocated instruction tuple from the combined `(:segment vm)` at absolute `(:pc vm)`; and `create-vm` with an empty image seeds `:images` with `[[empty-R 0 0]]` while `attach-image` leaves an empty-base VM's `:halted? true` and `:registers []` unchanged. | Specify in §5 that component instances add `base` to all exported pcs (`pc`, `site-pc`, `return-pc`, `:body-pc`), that `payload-of` always reads `inst` from the relocated combined `:segment`, and that `create-vm` / `attach-image` preserve the `[empty-R 0 0]` initial offset row and empty-base `:halted?`/`:registers` state.\\n\\n### Properties Passing Review\\n\\n1. **Core Wasm Execution Model (§1.1, §2.1, §2.2)**: i32 `ValueRef` locals with task-owned value arenas, body-indexed wasm functions with `br_table` intra-body dispatch, and a host trampoline keeping zero suspended guest frames on the native wasm stack.\\n2. **Contract \\u0026 Identity Preservation (§Decision, §2.3, §5)**: Exact preservation of register contract `\\\"r2\\\"` (version 4), 23 opcodes, `L`/`T` register banking, 6 in-band `live` operands, BLAKE3 `R` checksums, and `A` as the sole code identity with wasm modules treated strictly as disposable local caches.\\n3. **Continuation Model \\u0026 Multi-Shot Semantics (§3.1–§3.3)**: Exact `effects/continuation-payload` / return-frame shapes, multi-shot reified continuation invocation without native stack unwinding, and explicit separation of same-task `register-restore` image-membership checks from cross-task layout/transport gates.\\n4. **FFI Two-Step \\u0026 Scheduler Ordering (§4.1–§4.3)**: `ffi/require-call-pair!` before id minting or parking, correlated `[caller-token local-id]` call ids, `ok` vs `full` (`:request-sent`) two-step transition without duplicate appends, stale-wake key stripping via `ffi/response-wait-entry`, and `engine/run-loop` / `halted-with-empty-queue?` ordering.\\n5. **Append-Only Module Growth \\u0026 `IModuleKernel` Seam (§5)**: Relocation of `:pc`-kind operands, `[R offset length]` offset-table growth, preservation of in-flight absolute pcs across `attach-image`, isolated `spawn-module` state, and `reset` vs `load-image` code-space retention.\\n6. **Slice Structure \\u0026 Corpus Grounding (§6)**: Falsifiable W0–W6 gates properly accounting for open expressions and parked-id fixtures in `test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc` and full state/trace comparisons beyond B0 value normalization in `test/yin/vm/debruijn/register_test.cljc`.\\n7. **Design-vs-Implementation Discrepancy Analysis (§Decision)**: Accurate identification of stale return-frame code-space prose in `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md` §5.2, `:resource-updates` vs `:store-updates` in `yin.vm.engine.md`, and `vm/machine-data?` / `engine/encoder` continuation refusal behavior in current code.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":783.199579,\"num_turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":401254,\"output_tokens\":37238,\"thinking_tokens\":13219,\"cache_read_tokens\":2096572,\"total_tokens\":438492}}\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:9:## 1. Round-1 Finding Resolution Audit (Verified Against Body & Source Code)\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:13:### MAJOR-1 — Empty-`K` `:return` and `:return-result` continuation restore `:pc` preservation\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:21:### MAJOR-2 — Bidirectional synchronization between Clojure VM map fields and wasm linear memory across engine/public seams\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:30:### MAJOR-3 — `:call` `:host-fn` effect completion contract (`payload-of`, `park-entry-fns`, blocked `:pc` advance, post-effect `state` preservation)\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:43:### MINOR-1 — Continuation invocation check order and foreign-continuation error keyword\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:52:### MINOR-2 — `:halt` and empty-`K` `:return` must preserve existing `:registers`, `:frames`, and `:continuation`\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:59:### MINOR-3 — `effects/wait-entry-defect` scope and custody gate (`:yin.k/gate`) preservation\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:69:### MINOR-4 — Module attachment base offsets, combined-segment payload reads, and empty-base rows\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:80:## 2. Full-Document Consistency & Regression Check\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:89:## Verdict\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:91:APPROVE\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:93:### Findings Remaining\ncollab/1792331900000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r2.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:96:### Properties Passing Review\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:12:thread 01a14f30-ca56-7530-bb93-3a870eca7a7b). Review it independently: do not assume its\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:68:APPROVE or REQUEST CHANGES (or APPROVE WITH CHANGES), then per-finding rows of\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:8:## Overview\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:16:## Detailed Audit by Review Area\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:18:### 1. Semantic Fidelity (`register.cljc`, `debruijn_register_code.cljc`, `debruijn_register_effects.cljc`)\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:56:### 2. Continuation Correctness\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:67:### 3. Invariant Audit (`docs/design/datom.world.md`)\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:78:### 4. Blocking, Effects, and FFI (`engine.cljc`, `ffi.cljc`, `yin.vm.engine.md`)\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:99:### 5. Module Growth (`register.cljc`, `linker.cljc`, `yin.vm.linker.md`)\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:111:### 6. Slices and Acceptance (`corpus.cljc`, `register_test.cljc`)\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:118:### 7. Design Contradictions Verified Against Code\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:127:## Verdict\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:129:APPROVE WITH CHANGES\ncollab/1792330570048-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:139:### Properties Passing Review\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:5:## Decision and source precedence\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:11:The mandatory feature profile is **core wasm 1.0 with mutable globals and the original function table / `call_indirect` facility**: i32/i64/f32/f64, structured control, one non-shared wasm32 memory and one function table per module, single-result functions, active data/element segments. No externref or first-class reference values, typed function references, `call_ref`, `return_call`, WasmGC, bulk-memory/table instructions, multi-value, multi-memory, memory64, SIMD, exceptions, threads, component model or JS string builtins are assumed. The baseline table element kind used by `call_indirect` is not permission to emit the later reference-types instruction set. Copy/clear uses scalar loops; no implicit `memory.copy`, `table.set` or `table.grow` instruction may slip in through optimization. Mutable globals need not cross the import boundary; instance base coordinates can use immutable scalar imports.\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:25:### Rust-kernel authority, scope and explicit reconciliations\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:39:## 1. Value representation and linear-memory layout\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:41:### 1.1 Values: i32 references into a task-owned value arena\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:57:### 1.1.1 Three encoding domains; native hashing is mandatory\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:75:### 1.2 Proposed private memory ABI\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:96:### 1.2.1 Mandatory map ↔ memory synchronization\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:107:### 1.3 Ownership, spilling, and collection\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:115:## 2. Code generation strategy\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:117:### 2.1 Choice among the alternatives\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:131:### 2.1.1 LLVM sibling and shared equivalence law\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:135:### 2.2 Structuring algorithm\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:143:### 2.3 All 23 opcode lowerings\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:173:### 2.4 Exact host-function effect completion\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:185:## 3. Continuation capture and resume\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:187:### 3.1 Exact external/native shape\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:210:### 3.2 Restore algorithm and failure ordering\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:224:### 3.3 Host transport and different layouts\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:230:## 4. Blocking, effects, and FFI protocol\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:232:### 4.1 Embedding contract\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:242:### 4.1.1 Import ABI `yin.register.host.v1` (proposed, not existing source)\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:290:### 4.1.2 Deterministic service traversal (shared prerequisite)\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:310:### 4.2 Stream and park transitions\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:316:### 4.2.1 Custody gates are preserved engine semantics\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:328:### 4.3 FFI two-step, without duplicate sends\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:337:## 5. Modules and code growth\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:358:## 6. Implementation slices and acceptance gates\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:360:### Test harness common to every slice\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:372:### W0 — freeze the ABI and executable oracle\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:397:### W1 — pure register execution and body dispatch\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:405:### W2 — continuations and restore\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:413:### W3 — streams, shared scheduler and FFI\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:425:### W4 — attach, modules and lifetime correctness\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:435:### W5 — lane completion and release gate\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:441:### W6 — measured optimization, after correctness\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:445:### Explicit non-goals\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:449:No new opcode/contract version, alternate A→R allocator, native stack continuations, async-stack capture, universal cross-model continuation conversion, new portable continuation schema, full semantic VM feature parity beyond the established native fragment, direct arbitrary host FFI imports, WASI imports in the VM core, threads/shared memory, WasmGC dependency, numeric NaN boxing, a mandatory standalone host-free runtime for W5, or immediate JVM/Dart application bindings. Native Wasmtime/Wasmer embedding is required and is not a non-goal; optional WASI transports may live below the ABI. No promise to execute malicious wasm from the network: wasm is generated locally from admitted images. No optimization requirement before W5 correctness.\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:451:## 7. Risks and open questions\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:468:## Reviewer round 1 responses\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:485:## Revision log and reference check\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:499:## Round 3 changes\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:513:## Round 4 review responses\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:524:## Round 4 changes\ncollab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:535:## Round 5 changes\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:38:End with APPROVE / APPROVE WITH CHANGES / REQUEST CHANGES, per-finding rows, and\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:42:End with APPROVE / APPROVE WITH CHANGES / REQUEST CHANGES, per-finding rows, passing\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.stdout.log:1:{\"conversation_id\":\"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"The Round-4 independent second-architect review of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r4.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) has been written to [1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nAPPROVE\\n\\n### Findings Summary\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Section | Summary |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| None | — | — | All Round-1 and Round-3 findings are resolved. No open MAJOR or MINOR findings remain. |\\n\\n### Properties Passing Review\\n1. **Three Canonical Encoding \\u0026 Hash Domains (§1.1.1)**: Private ABI TLV wire messages (§4.1.1), executable register scalar/image encoding ([`debruijn-code/encode-scalar`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc#L410-L465) + [`rcode/register-hash`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc#L262-L271)), and Jing canonical CBOR content hashing ([`dao.jing.cbor/encode`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L1-L28) + [`jing/content-hash`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc#L171-L179) / [`jing/segment-key`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc#L182-L197)) are cleanly separated and gated against existing golden corpora so `:hash` (`R`), `:owner` ([`values/owner-tag`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L123-L130)), `:seal` ([`engine/seal-of`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L299-L302)), `:yin.k/profile` ([`vm/primitive-profile`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L338-L356)), and `:address` ([`module.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L92)) are bit-identical across CLJS, Wasmtime, and Wasmer.\\n2. **Unambiguous \\u0026 Interning-Invariant ABI Wire Codec (§4.1.1)**: Outer-only `u8 tag | u32 payload-byte-length (LE) | payload` framing, map/set sorting by recursively expanded canonical value bytes independent of `tag 13` arena references, canonical quiet NaN (`00 00 00 00 00 00 f8 7f` LE), and CLJS [`dao.jing.cbor/float64?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L472-L480) carrier + `-0.0` preservation ([`integer-host/exact-integer?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc#L51-L66)) eliminate cross-host encoding drift.\\n3. **Code-Verified \\u0026 Properly Phased Shared Traversal Order (§4.1.2)**: All unordered map/set traversal sites that mint IDs or choose diagnostics in [engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L847-L1124) (`encoder`, `encode-store`, `markers`, `lower-resources`, `receive-module`, [`resume-from-run-queue`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2295-L2315)) and [module.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L100-L169) (`module-entries`, `list-modules`) are accurately identified, existing explicit sorts ([`engine.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1009-L1106)) are preserved, the boundary between current kernel behavior and the planned shared prerequisite is explicit, and slice gates in W0, W3, and W4 are properly sequenced around it.\\n4. **Complete Slice Gates \\u0026 Preserved R2/R3 Architecture (§1–§7)**: Transport status and `NEED_SPACE` / `fetch-response` once-only retry conformance are gated in W0 and W3, Wasmer W1–W4 full-trace execution and bidirectional native↔CLJS module-slice parity are gated in W4, and all 23 opcode lowerings, map↔memory synchronization, continuation capture/restore, custody gates, FFI two-step, and core-wasm-1.0 portability invariants remain intact.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":3368.030767,\"num_turns\":5,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1213580,\"output_tokens\":107873,\"thinking_tokens\":49790,\"cache_read_tokens\":5583330,\"total_tokens\":1321453}}\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:4:Round 3. Two things happened after your APPROVE on the r2 plan:\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.prompt.md:45:End with APPROVE / APPROVE WITH CHANGES / REQUEST CHANGES plus per-finding rows and\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.stdout.log:1:{\"conversation_id\":\"f365ef1d-caa2-4379-8e96-51e64ca36af8\",\"status\":\"SUCCESS\",\"response\":\"The Round-3 independent second-architect review of [1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md) has been written to [1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\nAPPROVE WITH CHANGES\\n\\n### Findings Summary\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Section | Summary |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `MAJOR-1` | MAJOR | §1.1, §3.2, §4.1.1, §5, §6 | Explicitly require the Rust native service to implement [`debruijn-code/encode-scalar`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc#L410-L465) + [`rcode/register-hash`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc#L262-L271) and [`dao.jing.cbor/encode`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L1-L28) + [`jing/content-hash`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc#L160-L179) alongside the §4.1.1 ABI binary codec so `:hash` (`R`), `:owner` ([`values/owner-tag`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc#L123-L130)), `:seal` ([`engine/seal-of`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L299-L302)), `:yin.k/profile` ([`vm/primitive-profile`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L338-L356)), and `:address` ([`module.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L92)) match CLJS bit-for-bit. |\\n| `MAJOR-2` | MAJOR | §1.1, §4.1.1, §6 W0 | Specify in §4.1.1 that (1) map keys and set elements sort by canonical encoded value bytes (never by `tag 13` arena-reference bytes), (2) `tag 4` (`float64`) canonicalizes NaNs to `0x7ff8000000000000` ([`debruijn_code.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc#L232-L234), [`cbor.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc#L19-L20)) and preserves integral floats / `-0.0` on CLJS via `dao.jing.cbor`'s float64 carrier and [`integer-host/exact-integer?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc#L61-L66), and (3) string (`tag 5`) and collection (`tags 8..11`) payloads have a single unambiguous framing rule. |\\n| `MINOR-1` | MINOR | §4.1.1, §5, §6 W3–W4 | Specify a deterministic map-traversal order for [`engine/encoder`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L918-L922), [`engine/encode-store`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1044-L1046), [`engine/markers`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L978-L983) / [`lower-resources`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1017-L1028) / [`receive-module`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L1110-L1112), [`module/module-entries`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L100-L110) / [`list-modules`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc#L166-L169), and [`engine/resume-from-run-queue`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2304-L2306) so CLJS and Rust mint identical `:yin.k/c-N` and `:stream-N` IDs. |\\n| `MINOR-2` | MINOR | §4.1.1, §6 W0, W3, W4 | Move `NEED_SPACE` + `fetch-response` / `BAD_MESSAGE` / `ABI_MISMATCH` / `RESOURCE_LIMIT` transport tests into W0 and W3 (for effectful once-only retry), and add the Wasmer W1–W4 suite pass and native↔CLJS module-slice parity to W4's `Acceptance:` paragraph. |\\n\\n### Properties Passing Review\\n1. **R2 Body Integrity**: All Round-2 approved sections — all 23 opcode lowerings in §2.3 ([`debruijn_register_code.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc#L70-L151), [`register.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L624-L823)), §1.2.1 map↔memory synchronization, §2.4 host-function effect completion ([`run-call-effect`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L564-L580)), §3.1–3.2 continuation payload and restore ([`register-restore`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L403-L450), [`write-back`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L452-L469), [`return-transition`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L492-L518)), §4.2–4.3 stream/custody/FFI two-step ([`ffi-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc#L583-L617)), and the Round-1 response table — are retained unchanged without silent edits.\\n2. **Core-Wasm-1.0 Feature Profile \\u0026 WasmGC Non-Goal**: The baseline profile (`i32`/`i64`/`f32`/`f64`, structured control, one non-shared `wasm32` memory, one `call_indirect` table, mutable globals, active segments) is consistent throughout, avoids guest `table.grow`/`table.set`/`memory.copy`/`return_call` instructions, and rightly keeps WasmGC and `externref` as non-goals.\\n3. **Import ABI Framing \\u0026 `NEED_SPACE` Idempotence**: The `yin.register.host.v1` control-block layout (bytes `0..255`), single `exchange(control_ptr: i32) -\\u003e i32` import signature, and sequence-retained `NEED_SPACE` / `fetch-response` protocol cleanly decouple wasm execution from JS/browser assumptions and prevent duplicate effect execution on response buffer growth.\\n4. **Toolchain Pins \\u0026 Multi-Runtime Differential Harness**: W0 pins match the repository's [mise.toml](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/mise.toml#L6-L7) and [deps.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/deps.edn#L40) versions and require identical wasm binaries to execute with full step and ABI trace comparison across Node and Wasmtime from W1 and Wasmer through W4–W6.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":2791.112352,\"num_turns\":4,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1069082,\"output_tokens\":93852,\"thinking_tokens\":44593,\"cache_read_tokens\":4572402,\"total_tokens\":1162934}}\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:10:## 1. Verification of the Six Reconciliation Obligations (1a–1f)\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:23:## 2. Independent Audit of `docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md` vs. R5\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:25:### 2.1 Does R5 Demand Anything `rust-kernel.md` Forbids?\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:33:3. **`Send`/`Sync` and thread-local `Machine` ownership (`rust-kernel.md:138-142, 396-432, 553-564, 1243-1244`)**:\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:35:   - `r5` (`line 53`) explicitly matches this split: each task's `Machine` and `Value` arena are single-threaded (`!Send + !Sync`), while admitted `Image`s are shared via `Arc<Image>` and materialize constants per task.\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:46:### 2.2 Does `rust-kernel.md` Demand Anything R5's Slices Quietly Drop?\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:61:## 3. Enforceability of the \"No Second Port\" Rule Across W1–W4\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:70:## 4. Regression Check Against R1–R4 Approved Properties\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:79:## Verdict\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:81:APPROVE\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:83:### Findings Summary\ncollab/1792340500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r5.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:89:### Properties Passing Review\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:9:## 1. Verification of Round-3 Findings in R4\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:20:## 2. Audit of the Shared-Ordering Resolution (§4.1.2)\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:22:### 2.1 Code-Correctness of the Cited Unsorted Traversal Sites\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:40:### 2.2 Explicit Boundary Between Current Kernel Behavior and Planned Prerequisite\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:47:### 2.3 Phasing of Parity Gates Around the Shared-Ordering Prerequisite\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:55:## 3. Regression Check Against R2/R3 Approved Properties\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:66:## Verdict\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:68:APPROVE\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:70:### Findings Summary\ncollab/1792335500000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r4.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:76:### Properties Passing Review\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:9:## 1. Evaluation of Round-3 Review Questions (a–e)\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:11:### (a) Import ABI (`yin.register.host.v1`) Completeness and Freedom from JS Assumptions\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:27:### (b) Consistency of the Core-Wasm-1.0 Feature Profile and WasmGC Non-Goal\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:30:  - All post-MVP instructions and types (`externref`, `funcref` value manipulation, `call_ref`, `return_call`, WasmGC, `memory.copy`/`memory.fill`, `table.grow`/`table.set`/`table.copy`, multi-value, multi-memory, memory64, SIMD, exceptions, threads, component model, JS string builtins) are excluded from the baseline profile (line 11).\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:35:### (c) Falsifiability of Node/Wasmtime/Wasmer Parity Gates and Cross-Runtime Determinism\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:46:### (d) Slice Scope vs. Acceptance Gate Alignment\ncollab/1792333700000-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-review-r3.gemini-4-argon.findings.md:54:##