158), [§10.4](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1234-L1265), and [§12](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1294-L1300). |\\n| **1b** | Commits to the **single-engine-port rule**: native Rust/C/C++ service library is the `yin-value`, `yin-scalar`, `yin-image`, `yin-kernel`, `yin-prims`, `yin-engine`, and `yin-wire` crate workspace (`rust-kernel.md:1136–1145`), extended by a wasm handle/ABI facade and thin Wasmtime/Wasmer wrappers (`rust-kernel.md:991–995, 1308–1311`). | **RESOLVED** | Verified in [r5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L28-L29) (§0.2, line 28; §1, line 47; §2.1, line 53; §8, line 395) and cross-checked against [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1136-L1145), [§8.3](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L991-L995), and [§13.2](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1308-L1311). |\\n| **1c** | Aligns `i32` wasm value handles with the 16-byte `#[repr(C, u8)]` `Value` representation (`K-D2`, `rust-kernel.md:326–392, 1238–1244`) via a task-local handle table (`!Send + !Sync` `Machine`, `Send + Sync` `Arc\\u003cImage\\u003e`, safe `Clone`/`Drop`) and inherits the three Round-3 determinism rules from §4.1.1. | **RESOLVED** | Verified in [r5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L30-L31) (§0.2, line 30; §2.1, lines 53–55; §2.3, line 73) and cross-checked against [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L326-L432), [§5.5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L553-L564), and [§10.4 K-D2](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1238-L1244). |\\n| **1d** | Unifies **W0** and **`K0`** (`rust-kernel.md:1170–1171, 1185–1199`) into a single conformance kit exported from R4 that drives `(R4 CLJS reference, Rust kernel/interpreter, wasm)` and preserves all `K0` fixtures (`\\u003e65,535` registers, `:host-limit`, million-iteration tail, §7.3 tail-site matrix, 14 validator rules, refused-step atomicity). | **RESOLVED** | Verified in [r5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L31-L32) (§0.2, line 31; §6, lines 282–286; §7, lines 356, 362–365) and cross-checked against [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1170-L1199) and [§7.3](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L833-L869). |\\n| **1e** | Positions wasm lowering and `K4` LLVM lowering as sibling execution strategies under `rust-kernel.md:805–831` (§7.2 equivalence law) and node-local artifact-cache rules (`rust-kernel.md:997–1011, 1113–1122, 1261–1263`), with cross-strategy boundary fallback fixtures (`wasm -\\u003e Rust interpreter`, `wasm -\\u003e CLJS interpreter`). | **RESOLVED** | Verified in [r5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L32-L34) (§0.2, line 32; §3.2, lines 131–134; §6, line 284; §7, line 365; §8, line 395) and cross-checked against [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L805-L831), [§8.4](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L997-L1011), [§9.5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1113-L1122), and [§10.4 K-D7](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1261-L1263). |\\n| **1f** | Notes alignment with `rust-kernel.md` §11 Owner Questions (`rust-kernel.md:1280–1292`) and `C1`/`A3` (`rust-kernel.md:244–257, 1275–1277`). | **RESOLVED** | Verified in [r5](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792329904305-architect-register-wasm-lower-plan-r5.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L34-L37) (§0.2, lines 34–37) and cross-checked against [yin.vm.rust-kernel.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L244-L257) and [§10.6–§11](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md#L1275-L1292). |\\n\\n## 2. Contradiction Check \\u0026 Regression Verification\\n\\n- **No New Contradictions**: Checked `Value` layout and `unsafe` boundaries (`yin-value` only vs. `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` elsewhere), `Send`/`Sync` boundaries (`Machine` `!Send + !Sync`, `Arc\\u003cImage\\u003e` `Send + Sync`), `step` vs. `run` semantics across the Rust interpreter and wasm lanes, `u32` native index limits (`K-D2b`) vs. 64-bit wire PCs, `:live` in serialized `ReturnFrame`s, `live-exact-rule` recomputation at module admission, and deterministic allocation-triggered heap collection ([engine.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc#L2587-L2614)). Zero contradictions found.\\n- **No Regressions**: All previously approved Round-1 through Round-4 properties (`M1`–`M6`, `m1`–`m6`, `R2-M1`, `R2-m1`, `R2-m2`, `R3-m1`) remain intact in `r5`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verdict\\n\\n**`APPROVE`**\\n\\n- **Open MAJOR findings**: 0\\n- **Open MINOR findings**: 0\\n- **Summary**: `r5` is ready for implementation-phase gating after R4 lands.\\n\",\"duration_seconds\":10616.694967,\"num_turns\":6,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1444432,\"output_tokens\":125497,\"thinking_tokens\":57509,\"cache_read_tokens\":6442555,\"total_tokens\":1569929}}\nimages are lowered to LLVM IR and run as native code beside it.\n\nIt is subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md) (axioms and\ninvariants), [`yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`](./yin.vm.debruijn.register.md)\n(the register dimension, R, live sets, the sparse continuation),\n[`yin.vm.linker.md`](./yin.vm.linker.md) section 7.3 (the offset table,\n`attach-image`, closure lift and lower),\n[`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md) (content, refs,\nquery: what may and may not carry code), and\n[`yin.vm.semantic.md`](./yin.vm.semantic.md) (the CESK reading of a\nlinear image and the observer/loader/image split).\n\nIt refines, and in four named places amends,\n[`yin.vm.debruijn.targets.md`](./yin.vm.debruijn.targets.md), which\nalready decided that a Rust host exists (T1), that it interprets the\nregister image (T-D13), and that it starts pure (Level 0) and grows to\noffload (Level 1, T5). That document was written before R1, R2 and R4\nlanded. They have landed: the Clojure kernel implements all 23 opcodes of\ncontract `\"r2\"` (register contract version 4), the engine seam, the\noffset table, and the module kernel. Section 11 lists what this changes\nin the targets design; where the two disagree and this document does not\nsay so explicitly, the targets document governs.\n\nLine numbers were read from the working tree on 2026-10-03.\n\n---\n4. The K3 threshold for commissioning K4.\n5. K1 scalar classes: the eleven-class common domain first (targets\n   T-D6), with bigint, ratio and the float64 kind following?\n\nDEFERRED: a kernel-owned `repr(C)` counted object header that would\npermit inline retain and release (it moves the counting implementation\ninto an unsafe crate, so it needs a K3 number showing the out-of-line\ncalls matter); guaranteed tail calls between native bodies; SSA registers\nwith live-set write-back; guarded specialization and deoptimization;\nin-process JIT; cross-node artifact sharing; the Rust `dao.stream`\nclient and transports; WASM as an artifact target.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Risks\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
